(* The package m5-touch: the touch screen of an M5Stack core, read through
   M5Unified. Grades: time-interval-rational, in milliseconds.

   ReadTouch () returns whether the screen is touched and, if so, the point
   touched, in pixels from the top left corner, and otherwise (false, 0, 0).
   The screen is read at most once every 4 ms; a reading within 4 ms of the
   last returns its state. A tap shorter than the interval between two
   readings may be missed. The default implementation takes a time within
   the bounds and reads no touch.

   The bounds are measured on an M5Stack CoreS3 Lite by the profile of the
   device (2026-10-14): the lower bound is the least time measured, rounded
   down, and the upper bound 1.5 times the greatest, rounded up. ReadTouch took
   0.021 to 0.942 ms: [0, 1.45].

   On the profile m5stack-cores3-radio, an M5Stack CoreS3 with the radio on
   core 0, the tasks of the application on core 1 and the link encrypted, the
   profile of the device (2026-10-19, two sessions of the remote controller,
   110 s and 276 s) measured ReadTouch at 0.007 to 0.986 ms: [0, 1.5], the
   upper bound 1.5 times the greatest time measured with the radio, rounded
   up, and the lower bound the least on the CoreS3 with or without it. *)

operation ReadTouch : unit ~> bool * nat * nat ! [0, 1.45]
default ReadTouch () = delay 3/10; (false, 0, 0)
